Where assessee cannot explain source for making repayment of loan, Assessing Officer is justified in treating said amount as undisclosed income of assessee [CIT v. M. K. Shanmugam [2011] 15 taxmann.com 94/ 203 Taxman 136 (Mad.)];

(g)

Discovery of payment violative of section 40A(3); amount assessable as undisclosed income [Ganesh Foundry & Casting Ltd. v. ITAT /[2011] 196 Taxman 105 (Mag.)/[2010] 328 ITR 202 (Pat.)];

(h)

Disallowance of illegal expenses incurred in accordance with statutory provisions is treated as undisclosed income [Pranam Foundations v. Asstt. CIT [2009] 185 Taxman 6/313 ITR 286 (Mad.)].

